    "document_summary": "AIA Glow of Life is an AIA Singapore Private Limited critical illness plan designed specifically for women’s health needs and female-related critical illnesses. It provides a payout based on a “Female Dreaded Illness Benefit” for female cancers (including cancers of breast, cervix uteri, uterus, ovary, fallopian tube and vaginal/vulva), systemic lupus erythematosus (S.L.E) with lupus nephritis, and rheumatoid arthritis. It also includes a “Female Health Benefit” for osteoporosis (30% of coverage amount), urinary incontinence requiring surgical repair (5%), and carcinoma-in-situ of the female organs (20%), plus reconstructive surgery reimbursement due to accidents or burns (100%). Plans are tiered as Standard (S$25,000 coverage amount) and Executive (S$50,000). A second opinion on cancer is “Yes” for both. The brochure states a free health check-up once every two policy years (first available on the 3rd policy year), and a renewal bonus of 5% of the coverage amount for each renewal up to a maximum of five years. It also states that pre-existing conditions may result in no benefits and waiting periods apply for some conditions, with precise terms in the policy contract.",
